ures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"81f154de199b46a934e7e67ff68f6f34756be38152362b7eabec5049902540ae","event_uuid":"a4a72df9-a3f3-4233-a59d-1f55b834d5e1","position":{"commit_sha":"93cf0e39e68ea6c8378a91e188a691731e3bdd4d","position":"1786998691552083001-a4a72df9-a3f3-4233-a59d-1f55b834d5e1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"66411ea39f465f1abcfe7bdea2d165b9a4adc562be87c01f8719f9ecf12d2299","event_uuid":"49e799e9-ed87-4e08-8588-2ef2d6fb7d91","position":{"commit_sha":"0630619e5b4f34c9acb87290a2296111a69008df","position":"1786999183763647001-49e799e9-ed87-4e08-8588-2ef2d6fb7d91"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e22e0e7d8976039d0a9e37ce44e21098f2993fb45cce52e49e3de1f3909f2bfa","event_uuid":"8c7b996c-509e-48a0-b18d-b94ea9272a48","position":{"commit_sha":"d9fe310e5710ecaf391087df251e6d99d19a44c5","position":"1786999188397629001-8c7b996c-509e-48a0-b18d-b94ea9272a48"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented ac-process-gate (advisory 1-TURN, ac-text-quality, container+leaf). Live bounded-sanity eval: recall=1.0, false_accept=0.0, kappa=1.0 — both process-gate ACs (children-closed; tests/CI+plan-review pass) FIRED; both deliverable ACs (E2E tests for a named feature; plan-review criteria updated to a rubric) PASSED. Artifact: docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/ac_process_gate_sanity.json.\n\nCollateral (recorded in file_impact): (1) the 25th non-AGENT criterion under the test sandbox root tipped registry.chunk_by_facet into a trailing SINGLETON chunk (count % chunk-size == 1), which test_chunk_by_facet_packs_and_never_empty_for_input asserts against. Fixed the packer to a balanced pack (ceil(n/size) near-equal contiguous chunks, guaranteed [2,size] for n>=2), preserving facet adjacency; added a parametrized regression test proving no singleton for counts 2..39 (old packer stranded 7,13,19,25,31,37). (2) Per reviewer direction, REMOVED the stale-prone hard-coded criteria COUNT from docs/plan-review-gate.md + the registry docstring and from test_guides (kept the stable T1–T15 overlay-range check). (3) Golden pins updated: EXPECTED_ROUTING (advisory), measurement-provenance guide contract-line digest unchanged (reworded my rubric's operator-attested reference to avoid miscounting it as a contract line). make lint + make typecheck green; 236 focused tests pass.","timestamp":1786989430328474001}],"created_at":1786987707428774001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"64231c85-7c8f-4776-8eae-98139c33e7f8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"644a-50c0-1778-4e03"},{"link_uuid":"a6cabe58-b879-4fd7-88ba-04beeddd9c68","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8915-e10b-b7d7-4a2a"},{"link_uuid":"d8037074-95b5-4380-8688-defee44b0d68","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3b73-ca49-4aaf-46d8"},{"link_uuid":"154fe428-6cac-4a73-8e79-01d6af436792","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ae4e-027f-d4c8-45b0"},{"link_uuid":"44a1376c-3ea0-4642-b27a-9f8d69d1f657","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0165-9368-dc92-47be"},{"link_uuid":"510f8975-e58a-4bc7-853c-e0b5679f6a46","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b376-0341-0263-452c"},{"link_uuid":"65db6efb-e0c0-4325-9b2e-96a2331b8e1c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3b65-041d-730e-4223"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAcceptance criteria that merely restate a GENERIC development-process gate — one CI or rebar already enforces MECHANICALLY for every ticket regardless of subject — add no signal the completion verifier can act on. Examples seen in real tickets: \"all child tickets are closed\" (rebar's open-children guard enforces this structurally), \"all tests pass\" / \"CI is green\" (CI's Verified gate), \"plan review passes\" (the rebar/Gerrit plan-review gate). Such an AC would read identically on an ARBITRARY unrelated ticket. It cannot be truthfully evaluated by the completion verifier as ticket-specific work, wastes verifier effort, and can mislead it into gating close on a tautology. Plan review is the right place to catch these: an author-facing finding at plan time keeps them out of the accepted AC set, so the completion verifier is left with only ACs that meaningfully represent the delivered work.\n\nNo existing criterion covers this. `evidence-kind` classifies WHERE an AC's proof lives (codebase vs operator-attested) and would even ACCEPT \"all tests pass\" if tagged `[operator-attested]`; `E2` judges ambiguity; `ac-satisfiability` judges joint satisfiability; `E1` judges coverage/duplication. None asks whether an AC is a redundant mechanical gate.\n\n## Approach\nAdd ONE new plan-review LLM criterion, `ac-process-gate`, via the established built-in-criterion pattern (mirrors `necessity`, epic 6982/R4) — a 1-TURN, non-code-grounded, single-turn plan-text judgment, shipped ADVISORY (author-coaching) with promotion to blocking left as the documented dogfood-gated `criteria_routing.json` change in docs/plan-review-gate.md, exactly like the R1/R3/R4 family. The criterion visits every acceptance-criterion checkbox and FIRES on an AC whose ENTIRE completion predicate is a generic, ticket-agnostic process/tooling gate CI or rebar enforces for every ticket (children-closed; tests/CI/build/lint/typecheck pass; plan-review passes; completion-verifier passes; change merged/landed; commit-trailer/DCO present). It ACCEPTS (no finding) an AC that names or turns on THIS ticket's SPECIFIC deliverable — the artifact, behavior, contract, test, doc, config, or criterion the ticket produces — EVEN when tests/CI/plan-review are its subject (e.g. \"E2E tests are written covering feature X\", \"the plan-review criteria are updated to the new rubric Y\"). Discriminator/litmus: would this exact AC read and be satisfied IDENTICALLY on an arbitrary unrelated ticket? Yes -> generic gate -> FIRE; names/depends-on this ticket's specific deliverable -> PASS. Anti-FP: err toward SILENCE; an AC carrying any ticket-specific deliverable content passes.\n\nWiring follows the packaged pattern with no new machinery: (a) a rubric prompt file loaded by the existing da27 prompt library; (b) a routing entry in the packaged routing index; (c) membership in `CANONICAL_LLM`; (d) the regenerated tracked guide; (e) a committed bounded-sanity eval spec (the R4-style proving artifact). The criterion is in-process plan-review logic with no CI-provider trigger, so it is portable across environments with any or no CI provider.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_ac_process_gate.md` (NEW) — the rubric prompt (front-matter contract + discrimination body).\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json` — add the `ac-process-gate` routing entry (exec/facet/applies_at/posture/checklist).\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py` — add `ac-process-gate` to `CANONICAL_LLM` (NOT to `CODEBASE_GROUNDED`/`AGENT_TIER`).\n- `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` — regenerated (adds the `## ac-process-gate` section); regenerate-in-place, not hand-edited.\n- `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-ac-process-gate.eval.yaml` (NEW) — the committed bounded-sanity fire/no-fire corpus.\n- `tests/unit/test_ac_process_gate_criterion.py` (NEW) — deterministic registration/routing/front-matter/guide/eval-shape invariants.\n\n## Testing\n- The new deterministic unit module pins: canonical/1-TURN/not-grounded registration; non-orphan advisory routing with the container+leaf scope and the two-key checklist; the prompt front-matter contract; the regenerated guide section (`validate_criteria_guide == []`); the eval-spec shape (>=2 fire, >=2 no-fire, <=8 cases); and zero-wiring effectiveness-recorder auto-inclusion.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the focused unit module run clean; the packaged-routing and criteria-guide parity gates stay green.\n- Live bounded-sanity: `rebar criteria eval ac-process-gate --output json` fires on the process-gate ACs and passes the deliverable ACs; the result is committed as the run artifact.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A new plan-review criterion id `ac-process-gate` is a member of `registry.CANONICAL_LLM` and is absent from both `registry.CODEBASE_GROUNDED` and `registry.AGENT_TIER`, so `registry.exec_tier` resolves it to `1-TURN`.\n- [x] `registry.validate_packaged_routing()` returns `[]` with the new criterion present, i.e. `criteria_routing.json` carries an `ac-process-gate` entry whose `exec` is `1-TURN`, `default_posture` is `advisory`, `facet` is `ac-text-quality`, and `applies_at.scope` is `[\"container\",\"leaf\"]`.\n- [x] The `ac-process-gate` routing checklist has exactly two criterion-local sub-answers: a gate key that is not-applicable->PASS when the plan has no acceptance-criterion checkboxes, and a judgment key deciding whether each AC is a ticket-specific deliverable rather than a generic mechanical gate.\n- [x] `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_ac_process_gate.md` exists with front-matter `execution_mode: single_turn`, `category: plan-review-criterion`, and `dimension: ac-text-quality`, and its body both documents the ADVISORY posture and references `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n- [x] The rubric body enumerates the reject-set (children-closed; tests/CI/build/lint pass; plan-review passes; completion-verifier passes; merged/landed; commit-trailer/DCO) and the accept-set (an AC naming this ticket's specific deliverable, e.g. tests written covering a named feature, or a named criterion/rubric update), and states the \"reads identically on an arbitrary unrelated ticket\" litmus and the err-toward-silence anti-false-positive rule.\n- [x] `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` contains a `## ac-process-gate` section and `registry.validate_criteria_guide(<checkout>)` returns `[]`; `registry.explain_criterion(\"ac-process-gate\")` starts with `## ac-process-gate`.\n- [x] `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-ac-process-gate.eval.yaml` declares `prompt: plan-review-ac-process-gate` and a dataset of at most 8 cases with at least two `expect: finding` process-gate-AC positives and at least two `expect: pass` deliverable-AC negatives.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_ac_process_gate_criterion.py` asserts the registration, routing, checklist, front-matter, guide-section, eval-spec-shape, and effectiveness-recorder-auto-inclusion invariants above (existence and content of these invariants, independent of any CI run).\n- [x] [operator-attested] The live bounded-sanity eval (`rebar criteria eval ac-process-gate`) is run and its JSON result committed as `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/ac_process_gate_sanity.json`, with every must-fire case surfacing an `ac-process-gate` finding and every must-not-fire case surfacing none.\n  provenance: environment=rebar repo worktree (impl-ac-process-gate) with live AWS Bedrock access; principal=RebarBotNava (joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com); privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the eval invokes the same Bedrock plan-review model production plan-review uses over the committed fire/no-fire corpus; result kappa=1.0 committed as the run artifact.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_ac_process_gate.md","reason":"NEW rubric prompt for the ac-process-gate criterion"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json","reason":"add ac-process-gate routing entry"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py","reason":"add ac-process-gate to CANONICAL_LLM"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md","reason":"regenerated guide section for ac-process-gate"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-ac-process-gate.eval.yaml","reason":"NEW bounded-sanity eval corpus"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ac_process_gate_criterion.py","reason":"NEW deterministic invariants test"},{"path":"docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/ac_process_gate_sanity.json","reason":"committed live eval sanity run artifact"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review.py","reason":"regression test: chunk_by_facet never strands a singleton"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"drop stale hard-coded criteria count (keep overlay range)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_guides.py","reason":"stop pinning a hard-coded criteria count; keep overlay-range check"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_threshold_recalibration.py","reason":"pin ac-process-gate routing (advisory) in EXPECTED_ROUTING"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_guide.py","reason":"extracted guide-rendering cluster from registry.py to stay under the 800-LOC module-size cap (call-graph seam)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0165-9368-dc92-47be"],["relates_to","3b65-041d-730e-4223"],["relates_to","3b73-ca49-4aaf-46d8"],["relates_to","644a-50c0-1778-4e03"],["relates_to","8915-e10b-b7d7-4a2a"],["relates_to","ae4e-027f-d4c8-45b0"],["relates_to","b376-0341-0263-452c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"49e799e9-ed87-4e08-8588-2ef2d6fb7d91","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"83bf-5f42-6fb6-4abc","ticket_type":"task","title":"Plan-review criterion: flag mechanical process-gate ACs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1dffee85-5c43-4d0d-a0dd-41a4187e522c","9d2ebd87-0250-4ea9-af29-0784fbcd9531","e726c6fd-8d82-45c8-b0af-821fa79d5520","a6cabe58-b879-4fd7-88ba-04beeddd9c68","d8037074-95b5-4380-8688-defee44b0d68","154fe428-6cac-4a73-8e79-01d6af436792","44a1376c-3ea0-4642-b27a-9f8d69d1f657","510f8975-e58a-4bc7-853c-e0b5679f6a46","65db6efb-e0c0-4325-9b2e-96a2331b8e1c","3db089df-b01e-40ef-8de4-fa99079ccecc","b9b82819-a6a5-4f33-a3ff-cdf86db92a21","de0b2802-f5a1-4b40-b117-8f110d648d79","7aa0e9c4-4171-4c31-a4fa-1143d3639cd4","a4a72df9-a3f3-4233-a59d-1f55b834d5e1","49e799e9-ed87-4e08-8588-2ef2d6fb7d91","8c7b996c-509e-48a0-b18d-b94ea9272a48"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787011549858066779,"uuid":"0c76f3bf-1382-4caa-8218-eb779b447930"}